  "title": "Front Door vs Application Gateway",
  "description": "Choose between Azure Front Door and Application Gateway for global traffic management.",
  "order": 3,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "tags": ["azure", "front-door", "application-gateway", "global", "waf"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Problem Statement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "You have deployed your application in East US and West Europe. Users in Asia report 500ms+ latency. You need global load balancing, SSL offloading, and DDoS protection. Should you use Front Door or Application Gateway?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "What to Do"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use **Azure Front Door Standard/Premium** for global load balancing and acceleration. It routes users to the nearest region using Anycast, provides WAF, and integrates with CDN for static content."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "How to Implement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "ARM Template - Front Door with WAF",
        "language": "json",
        "code": "{\n  \"type\": \"Microsoft.Cdn/profiles\",\n  \"apiVersion\": \"2023-05-01\",\n  \"name\": \"fdProfile-prod\",\n  \"location\": \"global\",\n  \"sku\": { \"name\": \"Standard_AzureFrontDoor\" },\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"responseHeadersProfiles\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"securityHeaders\",\n        \"headersAction\": [\n          { \"headerActionType\": \"Overwrite\", \"headerName\": \"Strict-Transport-Security\", \"value\": \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Why Front Door"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Front Door** is globally distributed (65+ edge locations). **Application Gateway** is regional only. For multi-region apps, Front Door reduces latency by routing users to the nearest healthy endpoint."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
        "title": "Global Traffic Management",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Azure Front Door Standard/Premium",
            "description": "Global load balancer with WAF",
            "pros": [
              "Global edge network",
              "Anycast IP addresses",
              "SSL offloading at edge",
              "WAF integration",
              "CDN capabilities"
            ],
            "cons": ["Higher cost", "More complex routing rules"],
            "tags": ["Recommended for global apps"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Azure Application Gateway",
            "description": "Regional layer 7 load balancer",
            "pros": ["Lower cost", "WAF v2", "URL-based routing", "VNet integration"],
            "cons": ["Regional only", "No global acceleration"],
            "tags": ["Regional apps"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Azure Traffic Manager",
            "description": "DNS-based global traffic manager",
            "pros": ["DNS-level routing", "Low cost", "Any provider support"],
            "cons": ["DNS caching delays", "No WAF", "No SSL offloading"],
            "tags": ["DNS routing only", "Legacy"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
